{"id": "unknown-2026-06-10-004", "date": "2026-06-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["automotive_display"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Advanced semiconductor demand fuels Liying's fluorine recycling expansion", "content": "As demand for AI chips continued to surge, utilization rates at advanced semiconductor process lines kept climbing, making the circular-economy treatment of waste hydrofluoric acid and calcium fluoride sludge an essential service. Liying said the company's core strength lay in using intelligent production parameters to improve waste purity and regenerate the materials into green synthetic fluorite (calcium fluoride), helping semiconductor customers meet carbon reduction and ESG goals in advanced", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260610PD250/demand-circular-economy-chips-revenue-materials.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-10-005", "date": "2026-06-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "TXC eyes 30% optical module share by 2027", "content": "AI and optical communications demand are pushing frequency components toward higher frequencies, smaller sizes, lower power consumption, ultra-low jitter, and very high stability. Quartz component maker TXC sees AI and automotive as its main growth engines in 2026, and expects AI to account for 16% of full-year revenue this year. TXC currently holds a 20&ndash;30% share of the optical module market and aims to break above 30% in 2027.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260610PD245/txc-2027-automotive-2026-communications.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-06-10-006", "date": "2026-06-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Commentary: How AI boom gave Nokia and BlackBerry a second life", "content": "The artificial intelligence boom has created clear winners among semiconductor and memory manufacturers. Shares of companies such as Samsung Electronics, SK Hynix and Micron Technology have climbed as demand for AI memory chips continues to surge.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260610PD246/nokia-blackberry-infrastructure-demand-samsung.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-06-10-007", "date": "2026-06-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Commentary: Nvidia CEO visit spotlights Samsung in HBM supply race", "content": "Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang's multi-day trip to South Korea put the \"triangle relationship\" among Samsung Electronics, SK Hynix, and Nvidia over high-bandwidth memory (HBM) in the spotlight, even as he toured AI factories and sealed partnerships in robotics and physical AI. The visit underscored how HBM has become a strategic supply asset for Nvidia's expanding AI platform.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260610PD238/nvidia-samsung-hbm-ceo-sk-hynix.html", "type": "rss"}]}
